1:["$","$Ld",null,{"item":{"id":"build-the-diagram","number":"11","title":"Teach one path before the full system.","mode":"Visual overload","scale":"slide","dek":"Read the unknowns, blocks, and equilibrium targets before tracing twenty connections.","before":[{"kind":"image","title":"Two-asset HANK graph · PDF p. 72","image":"/originals/sequence-project-p72.png","alt":"A two-asset heterogeneous-agent New Keynesian model: seven computational blocks, three unknown paths, three equilibrium targets, and twenty labeled directed dependencies. Several long arrows cross the diagram.","id":"complete-hank-graph","sourcePage":"72"}],"after":[{"kind":"hank","stage":0,"title":"Three unknown paths. Three conditions to satisfy.","label":"TWO-ASSET HANK","lines":["Guess \\(r,w,Y\\); hold the exogenous paths \\(Z,r^{*},G\\) fixed.","The targets are residuals \\(H_1,H_2,H_3\\), each equal to zero at equilibrium."],"note":"22 endogenous variables reduce to three unknown paths.","revises":["complete-hank-graph"]},{"kind":"hank","stage":1,"title":"Inflation connects production to asset returns.","label":"PRICES AND RETURNS","lines":["Production supplies marginal cost \\(mc\\); the price Phillips block supplies inflation \\(\\pi\\).","Finance also takes \\((p,d,r)\\) from equity and \\(i\\) from monetary policy."],"note":"Equity values and monetary policy also enter the finance block.","revises":["complete-hank-graph"]},{"kind":"hank","stage":2,"title":"Household choices enter two equilibrium conditions.","label":"HOUSEHOLD CHOICES","lines":["Households take returns \\(r^a,r^b\\) and fiscal inputs \\(\\tau,w,N\\).","They supply asset demands \\(\\mathcal A,\\mathcal B\\) and the wage-setting statistic \\(\\mathcal U\\)."],"note":"Asset clearing also uses equity value; wage setting also uses fiscal inputs.","revises":["complete-hank-graph"]},{"kind":"hank-system","title":"Seven computations feed three equilibrium checks.","label":"THE COMPLETE SYSTEM","note":"Guessed paths: \\(r,w,Y\\) · Exogenous paths: \\(Z,r^*,G\\).","alt":"Seven ordered computations list every input and feed-forward variable. Production; price Phillips; fiscal; equity; monetary policy; finance; households. Three targets are Fisher, asset market, and wage Phillips residuals.","revises":["complete-hank-graph"]}],"diagnosis":"The source moves from simpler models to a much richer two-asset graph. At this jump, the audience must decode seven blocks and twenty dependencies while also learning which paths are unknown and which conditions close the model.","changes":["Identify the unknowns and equilibrium targets first.","Trace a short chain before following its branches.","Explain the household connections, then restore every original edge."],"preserved":"The complete source diagram returns unchanged in the final build: seven blocks, twenty labeled links, three unknown paths, and three equilibrium targets.","deferred":"The first teaching panels show selected dependency groups. The full graph, including equity, monetary-policy, and direct fiscal connections, remains the destination.","practice":"Choose one path through your most complicated diagram. Teach its inputs, intermediate objects, and destination before revealing the surrounding network.","principle":"Let the slide unfold","sourceType":"public","context":"NBER Summer Institute, July 2019. The authors already teach simpler directed graphs: a Krusell–Smith model on PDF p. 61 and a one-asset HANK model on p. 71. This revision adds a bridge into the two-asset graph on p. 72 (printed slide 24).","beforeCaption":"Two-asset HANK: seven blocks, twenty dependencies, three equilibrium targets.","afterCaption":"Four rebuilt views of the same model dependencies.","source":{"authors":"Adrien Auclert, Bence Bardóczy, Matt Rognlie, Ludwig Straub","title":"Using the Sequence-Space Jacobian to Solve and Estimate Heterogeneous-Agent Models","date":"July 2019","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shade-econ/sequence-jacobian/bcca2eff6041abc77d0a777e6c64f9ac6ff44305/docs/sequence_jacobian_slides.pdf","pages":"72"},"values":["Source inputs: exogenous Z, r*, G; endogenous unknown paths r, w, Y.","Seven blocks: production, fiscal, price Phillips curve, equity, finance, monetary policy, and heterogeneous households.","Three targets: Fisher equation H1, asset market clearing H2, wage Phillips curve H3.","The source graph has twenty labeled directed connections. Its complete original appears in the final better build."],"topic":"Computational macro","point":"The dependency graph becomes readable in three passes: equilibrium conditions, prices and returns, then households. A rebuilt computation table brings the complete system back together without crossing arrows."}}]
